  "headline": "Pairwise correlations persist: over a one-year window the pairs that moved together in one year are largely the pairs that move together in the next, with rank correlations of 0.48 to 0.68 across four index universes. That is far more stable than anything this app has measured about returns, which is why a correlation may inform position size where a return forecast may not. In the worst quarter of quarters for these markets the mean pairwise correlation is +0.14 higher than in the rest, so the diversification a correlation implies is smallest exactly when it matters most.",
