  "caveats": [
    "Today's index constituents, so every name measured is one that survived.",
    "A property of large-cap index members over this sample, not of any particular reader's portfolio, which may be concentrated in ways these universes are not.",
    "Non-overlapping windows, so the t-statistics do not share days. One history, one regime.",
    "The stress comparison conditions on each window's own return, which biases any correlation measured inside it (Forbes & Rigobon 2002). Whole windows are compared rather than selected days, which removes the worst of that, but not all of it."
